{"kind":"report","text":"# Why the hosted archive has not continued\n\nThis is a local source diagnosis of Main `b52ca7e3e99b6c592629c3544a943e440248a6cb`, not a read of the hosted archive row. The relevant archive code is unchanged in the current `origin/main` inspected here. The five published refs prove earlier sends; they do not reveal the writer's current row, wake or alarm. The observations supplied in request `66010f21` therefore do not identify one exact hosted stop reason.\n\nA large held journal does not, by itself, stop after its first pass. A confirmed partial pass keeps its receipt and clears its pending Mark. If the live head is later, confirmation writes an immediate continuation wake. Each alarm runs one pass and then sets the earliest remaining alarm. New sealed entries signal the writer; activating an admitted production object signals it too. The adaptive reader examines one next position at a time and can finish an earlier whole prefix under the same allowance. It does not require all 13,032 Room A entries in one pass.\n\nThere is, however, a durable terminal state. If planning or rebuilding returns a failure, the driver attempts to persist `stopped: {reason, where}` and a null wake. An ordinary exhausted/deadline exception instead returns retry; a failure while trying to save a stop can also leave retry rather than a stopped row. These paths must not be conflated. A persisted stopped row is checked before target resolution. New entries, object eviction, another alarm and the b52 deployment do not clear it. No reset/resume operation exists in the current ArchiveRows API or public room routes. Deleting the row is not a supported restart: it loses the bound receipt and can create a remote-ref conflict.\n\nA nonterminal retry is different. A pending Mark retains its exact bytes and attempts, with exponential delay from 1 second up to 300 seconds. Pre-Mark failures keep a durable wake; new entries do not shorten that backoff. A later alarm retries, checks an existing pending commit by ref read-back, and does not invent another accepted send. If a wake is missing but the row is not stopped, a genuinely new entry or production activation can signal it. Configuration/policy rejection can disable this driver instance and must be distinguished from either row state.\n\nConsequently, b52 resumes an ordinary due retry automatically if its configured target and owner remain available. It does not revive a persisted stop. There is no supported member command to restart a stopped row. A recovery for that state needs a separately reviewed owner change or narrowly specified administrative transition after the exact stored reason and receipt are read. This report proposes neither a mutation nor a retry.\n\n## Legacy publication at the reported sizes\n\nLegacy backfill is bounded by the **confirmed old prefix**, not the current live head. At the supplied receipts, Room A needs positions 0–1 and Site needs position 0. Both are below the original 4,096-entry ceiling. The first successful new published pass can include those complete legacy lists and its own list. Missing/pruned input, source proof, publication admission, ordinary work/metadata limits or the 30-second pass deadline can still refuse it. The total live sizes 13,031 and 3,710 alone neither prohibit backfill nor prove it will fit. Publication also requires a new position: an already caught-up v2 row returns idle, so quiet scopes may need a genuine new native entry before a new pass can carry legacy metadata. All five supplied live heads are beyond their receipts.\n\n## One nonsecret planner read\n\nRequest one owner-side, read-only **Room A archive scheduling snapshot**: current native head; whether `meta['archive-row-1']` and `meta['archive-wake-1']` exist and their byte sizes; row `confirmed.through`, `confirmed.layout`, `confirmed.anchorsPublished`, `pending` presence/through/commit/parent, `attempts`, `next`, `stopped.reason`; wake `pending`, `stopped`, `next`; and the actual `storage.getAlarm()` time. Do not return the pending manifest, publication bodies, entries, repository credentials or tokens. This is one finite diagnostic snapshot, not a request to expose a new public endpoint. No existing room read supplies it, so a supported owner-side read mechanism must be selected by the planner. A stopped reason, due retry plus alarm, or due wake without an alarm separates the main hypotheses. Without that snapshot, calling this a specific hosted overbudget stop would be speculation.\n\n## Source and local witness references\n\n- `packages/scope/src/archive-driver.ts`: `committed`, `wake`, `#pass`, `#confirmed`; explicit stop versus caught retry, pending read-back and immediate continuation.\n- `packages/scope/src/archive-row.ts`: `confirm`, `stop`, `wake`, `defer`, `signal`; durable stopped state and backoff-preserving wake index.\n- `packages/scope/src/object.ts`: constructor production activation/onSealed callbacks and `alarm`; `packages/scope/src/outbox.ts`: `Wakes.set` chooses earliest owner wake.\n- `packages/scope/src/archive-window.ts`: `openArchiveRootWindow` and `next`; scalar next-entry admission, not whole-live-history enumeration.\n- `packages/scope/src/archive-build.ts`: `planLegacyArchiveAnchors`; whole old confirmed prefix, same original allowance, no remote substitute for missing local inputs.\n- `packages/scope/src/archive-budget.ts`: 4,096 entries, 512 attempts, 64 nodes, 16,384 calls, 4 MiB metadata, 64 MiB input work and 30 seconds per pass; no top-up.\n- `packages/scope/test/archive-driver.test.ts`: scheduled partial-prefix continuation during 16 real turns; pre-Mark backoff survives eviction/new input; missing-input and rebuild-mismatch stops retain no alarm; pending SHA-1/SHA-256 reconstruction.\n- `packages/scope/test/archive-publication.test.ts`: genuine old receipt earns no coverage until a new whole-prefix publication; refusal writes no partial coverage. These are local fixture source witnesses, not a fresh test run or hosted-cause measurement.\n\nNo hosted call, operator material, runtime, code edit or test was used for this report.\n","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","report_sha256":"6ffba383dac6eb148bfae38447a901aa28ecc2b8ffa78a4084150c7f114182fe","scope":"Source-only diagnosis; no hosted calls, operator material, code changes or runtime."}}